# Sales ETL Pipeline in Python

A modular pipeline for the Extraction, Transformation, and Loading (ETL) of sales data. The project focuses on software engineering best practices applied to data engineering.

## Architecture and Best Practices Employed

- **Modularity:** Separate functions for Extract, Transform, and Load processes.
- **Clean Code:** Type hinting, exception handling (`try/except/raise`), and secure orchestration using `if __name__ == "__main__":`.
- **Traceability:** File-based logging system.
- **External Configuration:** Parameters managed via YAML files to avoid hardcoding (following Twelve-Factor App methodology).
- **Automated Testing:** Unit test coverage using `pytest` following the AAA (Arrange, Act, Assert) pattern.

## Getting Started

Follow these instructions to get a local copy of the project up and running for execution and testing.

### Prerequisites

- **Python 3.10+**
- **Git**

### 1. Clone the Repository & Setup Environment

```bash
git clone [https://github.com/LucasOgomes/sales-etl-pipeline.git](https://github.com/LucasOgomes/sales-etl-pipeline.git)
cd sales-etl-pipeline
python -m venv venv
venv\Scripts\activate
pip install -r requirements.txt

### 2. Configuration
Review and update config.yaml to set your desired file paths, log destinations, and target SQLite database parameters:

### 3. Run Automated Unit Tests
Validate transformation rules and edge-case behaviors (null handling, data typing) using pytest:
python -m pytest

### 4. Run the ETL Pipeline
To execute the end-to-end pipeline workflow:
python etl_vendas.py


Check logbook.log (or your configured log file) to inspect the execution trace and verify batch status.